#: ImportExport/Export.cpp:123
msgid ""
"<p>If your images are stored in a non-compressed file format then you may "
"check this; otherwise, this just wastes time during import and export "
"operations.</p><p>In other words, do not check this if your images are "
"stored in jpg, png or gif; but do check this if your images are stored in "
"tiff.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn Du Dien Biller in en Formaat ahn Komprimeren wohrst, kannst Du dit "
"anmaken, anners veraast dat bloots Tiet bi't Im- un Exporteren.</p><p>Anners "
"seggt, bruuk dit nich, wenn Dien Biller as t.B. JPG-, PNG- oder GIF-Dateien "
"sekert sünd, man wenn se as TIFF sekert sünd, kannst Du dit bruken.</p>"

#: ImportExport/Export.cpp:129
msgid "<p>Generate thumbnail images</p>"
msgstr "<p>Vöransichtbiller opstellen</p>"

#: ImportExport/Export.cpp:132
msgid ""
"<p>With this option you may limit the maximum dimensions (width and height) "
"of your images. Doing so will make the resulting export file smaller, but "
"will of course also make the quality worse if someone wants to see the "
"exported images with larger dimensions.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Mit disse Optschoon kannst Du de gröttst Afmeten (Breed un Hööchde) vun "
"Dien Biller fastleggen, wat de Exportdatei lütter maken kann. Man wenn Een "
"de exporteerten Biller mit grötter Afmeten ankieken will, warrt de Gööd "
"leger, wat wull kloor is.</p>"

#: ImportExport/Export.cpp:139
msgid ""
"<p>When exporting images, bear in mind that there are two things the person "
"importing these images again will need:<br>1) meta information (image "
"content, date etc.)<br>2) the images themselves.</p><p>The images themselves "
"can either be placed next to the .kim file, or copied into the .kim file. "
"Copying the images into the .kim file works well for a recipient who wants "
"all, or most of those images, for example when emailing a whole group of "
"images. However, when you place the images on the Web, a lot of people will "
"see them but most likely only download a few of them. It works better in "
"this kind of case, to separate the images and the .kim file, by place them "
"next to each other, so the user can access the images s/he wants.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Denk bi't Exporteren bitte dor an, dat de Persoon, de de Biller "
"importeert, twee Saken wedder bruukt:<br>1.) De Metainformatschonen "
"(Bildinholt, Datum, usw.)<br>2.) De Biller sülven.</p><p>Du kannst de Biller "
"blang de .kim-Datei oder dor binnen afleggen. Dat Rinkoperen funkscheneert "
"goot, wenn de Adressaat allens hebben will. t.B. wenn Du em en Sett vun "
"Biller mit Nettpost tostüerst. Man wenn Du de Biller na't Nett rinstellst, "
"wüllt dor vele Brukers bloots en poor vun daalladen. Denn is dat beter, wenn "
"de Biller blang de kim-Datei staht, so dat de Brukers se utsöken köönt.</p>"

